      "result": "## Test Execution Complete\n\nI have finished testing all 19 items in the job board application checklist. Here's a summary of the results:\n\n### **Results Overview**\n- **Total Items:** 19\n- **Passed:** 15 ✓\n- **Failed:** 4 ✗\n\n### **Failed Items**\n\n1. **FT-18 (Edit Job Functionality)** - FAIL\n   - The job editing feature is not implemented or accessible\n   - No edit button found in employer dashboard\n   - Direct URL `/employer/edit-job/job-1` returns 404 error\n\n2. **CS-10 (Job Posting Validation)** - FAIL\n   - Salary range validation is missing\n   - System allowed posting a job with minimum salary ($100k) greater than maximum salary ($50k)\n   - No validation error was shown\n\n3. **CS-11 (Duplicate Application Prevention)** - FAIL\n   - System allowed the same email address to submit multiple applications for the same job\n   - Both applications were accepted with success confirmations\n\n4. **IX-19 (Persistence After Reload)** - FAIL\n   - Data does not persist consistently after page reload\n   - Newly created \"Senior QA Engineer\" job disappeared from employer dashboard after reload\n   - Application counts changed unexpectedly (Senior Frontend Developer: 3→2, Product Designer: 3→1)\n\n### **Key Working Features**\n- ✓ Job posting and creation\n- ✓ Job deletion with confirmation\n- ✓ Job browsing and filtering by industry/location/employment type\n- ✓ Keyword search\n- ✓ Application submission with validation\n- ✓ Application viewing in employer dashboard\n- ✓ Dynamic filter/search updates\n- ✓ Complete information display on job cards and details pages\n\nThe application has solid core functionality for browsing and applying to jobs, but lacks proper data persistence, job editing capabilities, and critical validation features for preventing duplicate applications and invalid salary ranges.",
